Consider the recursive functions represented by the following code segment: int bar(int n) {
  if (n == 1) return 0;
  else return 1 + bar(n/2);
 }
 int foo(int n) {
  if (n == 1) return 1;
  else return 1 + foo(bar(n));
 } The smallest positive integer n for which [latex]\text{foo(n)}[/latex] returns [latex]5[/latex] is ________. (answer in integer) Note: Ignore syntax errors (if any) in the function.

Consider the following program snippet. Assume that the program compiles and runs successfully. Further, assume that the fork() system call is always successful in creating a process. int main () {
  int i;
  for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  	if (fork() == 0) {
  		continue;
  	}
  	break;
  }
  printf("Hello!");
  return 0;
 } The total number of times that the printf statement gets executed is ________. (answer in integer)

